<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42932" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">schĕdĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχέδιος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>made suddenly</i>
			or <i>off-hand; hastily put</i> or <i>thrown together;</i> hence, as in the Greek <i>subst.</i>, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">schĕdĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχεδία</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς</span>),
				<i>a raft</i>, <i>float</i>,
			constructed in haste, <i><span class="en">Dig. 14, 1, 1, § 6</span></i>; cf. Fest.
			pp. 334 and 335 Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">schĕdĭum</span></b> ,
				ii, n. (sc. carmen), <i>an extemporaneous poem</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lucilianae humilitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 4 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. de Deo Socr. p. 364, 34</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 7 praef.</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 3</span></i>; cf. Fest. l.
		l.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
